// sim/personas.mjs — six bot personas, each with a genuinely different
// memory-writing style, each GENERATED BY A REAL MODEL over a real task.
//
// WHY STYLES AND NOT SIZES. The library's promotion gate counts SESSIONS and
// DOMAINS. Uniform personas all cross that gate on the same inputs, so a uniform
// suite measures one point in the space and calls it coverage. The styles below
// are chosen to attack different parts of the pipeline:
//
//   chatty       → parses fine, promotes fine, but floods: does the merge
//                  survive volume, and do near-duplicate names fragment?
//   terse        → parses fine, promotes almost nothing: is the *useful* one
//                  getting lost in the noise, or is recall genuinely empty?
//   noisy        → claims that are status chatter; does assessClaim reject the
//                  narration without eating the one real claim beside it?
//   degenerate   → structurally broken: prototype-key headers, 1MB blocks,
//                  fences-in-fences, unicode edges. Must not throw, must not
//                  hang, must not pollute Object.prototype.
//   hostile      → the exact inputs that broke the real deployment, isolated so
//                  a failure names its trigger instead of "degenerate".
//   knowledgeable→ MUST survive. If genuinely useful cross-domain claims do not
//                  promote, the filter is too aggressive and that is the most
//                  expensive possible bug.
//
// TOPIC POOL. Real content — agent orchestration, security findings, deploy
// practice, memory architecture, Josh's actual decisions. Lorem ipsum cannot
// surface a relevance bug, and a relevance bug is the one this whole card
// exists to catch.
//
// FOUR SESSIONS PER PERSONA. promotion's established bar is 3+ sessions AND 2+
// domains (computeStatus). Three sessions would sit exactly on the boundary, so
// four: three to cross it, one to prove the union is stable on replay.

export const SESSION_DATES = ['2026-10-11', '2026-10-12', '2026-10-13', '2026-10-14'];

// Realistic, dated, specific. Nothing here is invented filler: these are the
